{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that the parameter priors for `alpha`, `beta`, and `sigma` appear before the likelihood statement. This preserves the same posterior/log density because Stan sampling statements add commutative log-density terms. No data fields were added or changed. Context data `N`, `J`, `county`, `x`, and `u` are not protected; they are used only as sizes, indices, or predictors.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N; // observations
  int<lower=1> J; // counties
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] y; // radon
  vector[N] x; // floor
  vector[N] u; // uranium
}
transformed data {
  matrix[N, 2] xs = [x', u']';
}
parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  vector[2] beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] alphas = alpha[county];
}
model {
  alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 10);
  y ~ normal_id_glm(xs, alphas, beta, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":1,"county":[1],"u":[6.951264832519053],"x":[6.162520723711106],"y":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
